<section id="module-wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd">
<span id="wissenai-extract-tables-tatr-tsd-module"></span><h2>wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd module<a class="headerlink" href="#module-wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<p>Module for table detection using table transformer model.
Import the function tsd_infer for inferencing, visualization and generating cropped images.</p>


<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd.tsd_infer">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">tsd_infer</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">str</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">device</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">str</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">detection_class_thresholds</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">dict</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">crop_padding</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">int</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">max_size_value</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">int</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">visualize</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">bool</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">visualize_dir</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">:</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n"><span class="pre">str</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span> <span class="sig-return"><span class="sig-return-icon">&#x2192;</span> <span class="sig-return-typehint"><span class="pre">Tuple</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">[</span></span><span class="pre">List</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">[</span></span><span class="pre">Image</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">]</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">,</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="pre">List</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">[</span></span><span class="pre">Dict</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">[</span></span><span class="pre">str</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">,</span></span><span class="w"> </span><span class="pre">object</span><span class="p"><span class="pre">]</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">]</span></span><span class="p"><span class="pre">]</span></span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/extract/tables/tatr_tsd.html#tsd_infer"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd.tsd_infer" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Function that performs inferencing of test images containing tables in them, using the table tranformer for 
table detection model.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): Path to the image to be used for inferencing
device (str): cpu or cuda
detection_class_thresholds (dict): Set threshold for classes such as table and table rotated.Usage reference below,
detection_class_thresholds = {“table”: 0.5,”table rotated”: 0.5,”no object”: 10}
crop_padding (int): padding to be added to each cropped image from the region of image where table is detected
max_size_value(int): Value for image resizing used by tatr model.Standard value is 800
visualize (bool): Whether bounding box visualization is required or not
visualize_dir (str): If bounding box visualization is required, provide the path(including file name) where 
visualized images are to be saved</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>Tuple[List[Image.Image], List[Dict[str, object]]]:</dt><dd><ul class="simple">
<li><p>A list of cropped images. Each item in the list is an instance of <cite>PIL.Image.Image</cite>.</p></li>
<li><dl class="simple">
<dt>A list of dictionaries where each dictionary contains:</dt><dd><ul>
<li><p>‘score’ (float): The confidence score of the detection.</p></li>
<li><p>‘label’ (str): The label or class of the detected table.</p></li>
<li><p>‘bbox’ (Tuple[int, int, int, int]): (xmin,ymin,xmax,ymax) indicating top left and bottom right corner of image.</p></li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
</li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd.visualize_detected_tables">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">visualize_detected_tables</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">img</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">det_tables</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">out_path</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">None</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/extract/tables/tatr_tsd.html#visualize_detected_tables"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.extract.tables.tatr_tsd.visualize_detected_tables" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Function that will draw bounding boxes around the tables detected in the image as
predicted by the model</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>img (_type_): _description_
det_tables (_type_): _description_
out_path (_type_, optional): _description_. Defaults to None.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>_type_: _description_</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

</section>
